<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RM_LiquidDef_AstrofuelAdoption.xml     HAND-AUTHORED (LIQUID_TYPES_MOD_1)
  ============================================================================
  design/RimMandrake/liquids_framework_design.md §3: "Astrofuel — adopts
  Vanilla Gravship Expanded — the VGE_Astrofuel* net (pipe/tap/valve/drain/
  giant tank/synthesizer) already exists in the campaign dump; optional-
  checked, supported when present" and §8's own measured line: "VGE_Astrofuel*
  full pipe net present — astrofuel row adopts, builds nothing."

  Hand-authored rather than added to LIQUID_DEF_ROWS (generate_liquid_suite.py)
  because that table emits UNCONDITIONAL <RimMandrake.FlowWorks.LiquidTypes.
  LiquidDef> defs straight into RM_LiquidDefRegistry.xml — a hard <bottle>
  reference to VGE_Astrofuel (a ThingDef field, confirmed by reading
  Source/LiquidTypes/LiquidDef.cs's LiquidBottledForm.bottle) would be an
  unresolved cross-reference (a red Player.log error) the moment Vanilla
  Gravship Expanded is inactive — this item's own registry is supposed to
  load clean under "minimal list + the mod" alone. Same reasoning the compat
  index's own docstring already gives for the acid/slime/normal-water rows:
  a patch that references an absent target must be PatchOperationConditional-
  guarded, never a hard field.

  So: no static LiquidDef ships for astrofuel at all when VGE is absent —
  matching the design's own "supported when present", not "always present,
  broken when absent". When VGE_Astrofuel (the ThingDef) exists, this ADDS a
  brand-new top-level LiquidDef into /Defs, entirely inside the conditional
  match, so by the time cross-references resolve VGE_Astrofuel is already
  known to exist in the same patch pass — the identical ordering the existing
  compat-index Operations already rely on.

  packageId confirmed via the frozen dump (OFFICIAL-2026-08-29,
  defs/ThingDef.json): VGE_Astrofuel -> modName "Vanilla Gravship Expanded -
  Chapter 1", packageId "vanillaexpanded.gravship". Gated on the def's own
  existence (the established convention in this mod's compat patches), not
  PatchOperationFindMod, so no packageId string needs to stay in sync with a
  donor mod's own naming.

  Values, same minimal-invention posture as the chemfuel row (an adopted
  item, not a re-authored liquid): viscosityClass/pH [INVENTED, no engine
  field measures either for an adopted item] mirror chemfuel's own row
  exactly. flammable=true is cited (astrofuel explodes/burns per its own
  CompProperties_Explosive/Flammable in the frozen dump). No terrainSuite,
  canalFluid or pipeResource — the design's own "adopts, builds nothing":
  VGE's astrofuel net is its own pipe system, not something this mod feeds
  or drains before a WORLDMAP_LIQUID_TAGS_1-class item (or VGE's own pipe
  net) decides to wire it, out of scope here.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="VGE_Astrofuel"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs</xpath>
      <value>
        <RimMandrake.FlowWorks.LiquidTypes.LiquidDef>
          <defName>RM_Liquid_Astrofuel</defName>
          <label>astrofuel</label>
          <description>Refined gravship propellant, adopted as-is — the Vanilla Gravship Expanded item already is this liquid's bottled form.</description>
          <viscosityClass>Water</viscosityClass>
          <pH>7</pH>
          <flammable>true</flammable>
          <bottled>
            <bottle>VGE_Astrofuel</bottle>
            <unitsPerBottle>1</unitsPerBottle>
          </bottled>
        </RimMandrake.FlowWorks.LiquidTypes.LiquidDef>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
